  ⚠ Approve proposal p-0005 and apply these changes to /srv/files-example?                                              
                                                                                                                        
  Yes marks the proposal as approved and then makes the changes shown, the way adding the folder by hand makes them.    
  Right before that the proposal and its effect are read again, and nothing is applied if either differs from what you  
  saw. The result is kept on the proposal.                                                                              
                                                                                                                        
    folder: /srv/files-example                                                                                          
    case: files (files without a repository; a first commit takes the listed files)                                     
    owner: root, group: root, mode: 0755                                                                                
    the service can write it: no                                                                                        
    permissions are set: yes                                                                                            
                                                                                                                        
  Files of the first commit (2)                                                                                         
    demo/.env                                                                                                           
    demo/compose.yaml                                                                                                   
                                                                                                                        
  Left out (1), recorded only in .git/info/exclude                                                                      
    demo/data: bind-mount (stack demo)                                                                                  
                                                                                                                        
  Stacks (1)                                                                                                            
    demo (folder demo)                                                                                                  
      works: deploy                                                                                                     
      does not work: backup                                                                                             
      warning secrets-env-not-ignored: secrets.env is not listed in .gitignore                                          
      conflict: the container demo-app-1 of the project old-demo runs in the folder                                     
                                                                                                                        
  Changes after yes                                                                                                     
    A git repository is started with branch main and a first commit of the listed files as qhost; no file in the folder 
    is written. It is taken over as a local stack folder.                                                               
    3 paths get the group of the service account with group write; the owner stays                                      
    The folder is added to the systemd drop-in of the service, which restarts once.                                     
                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
